      "rev_n_4_4842ee_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_4842ee_1",
        "node_id": "n_4_4842ee",
        "thought_text": "The error in the previous reasoning was in the calculation of the marked cells. The approach of subtracting the overlap area from the total area is incorrect. Instead, we should calculate the total area of the entire field minus the area of the ship, which is (w1 + w2) * (h1 + h2) - (w1 * h1 + w2 * h2). This accounts for the fact that the ship occupies a rectangular area on the field, and we need to exclude this area from the marked cells.",
